  "question": {
    "text": "A square loop of edge length $2 \\mathrm{~m}$ carrying current of $2 \\mathrm{~A}$ is placed with its edges parallel to the $x$ $y$ axis. A magnetic field is passing through the $x-y$ plane and expressed as $\\vec{B}=B_0(1+4 x) \\hat{k}$, where $B_0=5 \\mathrm{~T}$. The net magnetic force experienced by the loop is _______ $\\mathrm{N}$."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "160",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0025_d6092972d25f.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{x}=0)=\\mathrm{B}_0, \\quad \\mathrm{~B}(\\mathrm{x}=2)=9 \\mathrm{~B}_0 \\\\ & \\text { Also, } \\mathrm{F}=\\mathrm{i} \\ell \\mathrm{B} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{F}_1=\\mathrm{i} \\ell \\mathrm{B}_0 \\quad \\& \\quad \\mathrm{~F}_2=9 \\mathrm{i} \\ell \\mathrm{B}_0 \\\\ & \\mathrm{~F}=\\mathrm{F}_2-\\mathrm{F}_1=8 \\mathrm{i} \\ell \\mathrm{B}_0=8 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 5 \\\\ & \\mathrm{~F}=160 \\mathrm{~N}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}